  "details": "This is mostly driven by my desire to make it easier to add gun-style props to avatars (or anything else that would benefit from being able to detect the trigger).\nI should preface this by noting that am only speaking in terms of Oculus controllers here, because that's my only personal experience. (I have heard informally that Index controllers may already behave in a similar fashion to how I am about to describe though).\nCurrently, the fist gesture is activated by is just the grip trigger being depressed, with analog control over the gesture weight. This however makes it very difficult to simulate interactions that require a trigger, because once in the fist state, the primary trigger has no effect.\nMy proposal is to have the grip trigger only provide a gesture weight range of 0 to 0.9, and the remaining 0.1 is provided by depressing the primary trigger. This would allow for detection of that range for logic requiring trigger action, while still being mostly backwards compatible with existing avatars.",
